# /etc/cron.d/archie-live-tree-acl
#
# Re-apply write ACLs to host_commands/completed/ once an hour.
#
# WHY THIS IS NEEDED
#   archie_platform runs as uid 0 and writes these command-result files with an
#   explicit chmod(644). On a file that already carries an ACL, chmod rewrites
#   the *mask* instead of the named user entry — so it strips u:1000:rw while
#   the mode string still reads as a plain 644. The files revert to root-only
#   after every platform write. This job puts the grant back.
#
# WHY IT IS SCOPED TO ONE DIRECTORY
#   A full-tree re-walk is ~227k entries and would reach into
#   kytran-server-manager/data/postgres/, i.e. a live database directory. A
#   timer has no business walking that on a schedule. The development workflow
#   (source, .git, repos, scripts, website data) was fixed once by the
#   tree-wide ACL and does not decay, because git, editors and build steps write
#   without an explicit chmod and inherit correctly.
#
#   This directory is gitignored (.gitignore:141) platform output that nobody
#   edits, so the job is housekeeping, not a correctness dependency.
#
# INSTALL
#   sudo cp scripts/archie-live-tree-acl.cron /etc/cron.d/archie-live-tree-acl
#   sudo chown root:root /etc/cron.d/archie-live-tree-acl
#   sudo chmod 644 /etc/cron.d/archie-live-tree-acl
#
#   The installed name must be dot-free — Debian's cron silently ignores
#   /etc/cron.d entries whose names contain a dot, which is why the repo copy is
#   *.cron but the installed file is not.
#
# VERIFY IT IS PICKED UP
#   sudo cat /var/log/syslog | grep CRON | tail -5
#   Or run the exact command by hand first:
#   sudo /mnt/archie_brain/scripts/fix-live-tree-ownership.sh --apply-acl \
#        --path host_commands/completed
#
# SILENCE
#   --quiet means a successful run mails nothing. You will only be told if
#   something is wrong (setfacl missing, path gone, uid resolution failed).
#
# TO DISABLE
#   sudo rm /etc/cron.d/archie-live-tree-acl      # nothing else depends on it

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# :17 past the hour — off-peak so it does not pile onto every other cron job
# that fires at :00.
17 * * * * root /mnt/archie_brain/scripts/fix-live-tree-ownership.sh --apply-acl --path host_commands/completed --quiet
